From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Gerard Marull-Paretas <gerard@teslabs.com>
Date: Fri, 27 Nov 2026 15:42:42 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] dt-bindings: display: st,stm32-dsi: Add the wrapper interrupt
 and TE pin

The DSI host wrapper has an interrupt, which reports the tearing effect
and the end of a refresh in adapted command mode. A panel may also
report its tearing effect on a pin rather than over the link.

Allow the interrupt, and a default pin control state for the TE pin.

PebbleOS describes the DSI host of the STM32H747 with them.
---
 display/st,stm32-dsi.yaml | 14 ++++++++++++++
 1 file changed, 14 insertions(+)

diff --git a/display/st,stm32-dsi.yaml b/display/st,stm32-dsi.yaml
index 5356005..8b1c216 100644
--- a/display/st,stm32-dsi.yaml
+++ b/display/st,stm32-dsi.yaml
@@ -23,6 +23,12 @@ properties:
   reg:
     maxItems: 1
 
+  interrupts:
+    maxItems: 1
+    description:
+      The wrapper interrupt, which reports the tearing effect and the end of a
+      refresh in adapted command mode.
+
   clocks:
     items:
       - description: Module Clock
@@ -44,6 +50,14 @@ properties:
     items:
       - const: apb
 
+  pinctrl-0:
+    description:
+      The TE pin, when the panel reports its tearing effect on it rather than
+      over the link.
+
+  pinctrl-names:
+    const: default
+
   phy-dsi-supply:
     description:
       Phandle of the regulator that provides the supply voltage.
